      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, if your team intends to leave the international transit zone, even for a few hours, it almost certainly triggers a full entry requirement, not just a simple transit pass. Most airports require travelers entering the city proper to possess the proper visa beforehand, regardless of the stopover duration. Look specifically for information on \"short-term stay\" or \"tourist entry\" requirements for those countries. It's best to pre-arrange necessary visas or use electronic pre-approval systems before they even approach immigration.",
      "source": "target",
